// A nonatomic store does not take part in RC11's synchronises-with.
//
// MoRDor's own test. RC11's sw runs from a release through a write of mode
// relaxed or stronger, `rs`, to a read of mode relaxed or stronger and on to an
// acquire. Here the only write between the two fences is nonatomic, so there is
// no sw edge, nothing orders `y := 1` before `r2 := y`, and r2 may still read 0.
//
// Mode matching asked all three mode fields of an event, and a store's unused
// read and fence modes default to relaxed, so the nonatomic store matched and
// the fences synchronised. That forbade this outcome.
// nonatomic-store-no-sync-relaxed.lit is the control.
x := 0; y := 0;
{
  y := 1;
  fence(release);
  x.store(1, nonatomic)
} ||| {
  r1 := x.load(relaxed);
  fence(acquire);
  r2 := y
}
%%
allow (r1 = 1 && r2 = 0) [RC11]
